msgid "<0>-ke</0> makes a thing small or dear. It usually joins the genitive."
msgstr "<0>-ke</0> makes a thing small or dear. It usually joins the genitive."

msgid "<0>-ke</0> makes something small or dear, and usually joins the genitive: <1>majake, tükike, linnake</1>. It changes like <2>-ne</2>: <3>majakese, majakest</3>."
msgstr "<0>-ke</0> makes something small or dear, and usually joins the genitive: <1>majake, tükike, linnake</1>. It changes like <2>-ne</2>: <3>majakese, majakest</3>."

msgid "<0>-ke</0>: a small one."
msgstr "<0>-ke</0>: a small one."

msgid "<0>-lik</0> makes an adjective, like it or having it: <1>sõbralik, kohalik, ohtlik</1>. Learn each one, since the stem before it varies."
msgstr "<0>-lik</0> makes an adjective, like it or having it: <1>sõbralik, kohalik, ohtlik</1>. Learn each one, since the stem before it varies."

msgid "<0>-lik</0> makes an adjective: like it, or having it."
msgstr "<0>-lik</0> makes an adjective: like it, or having it."

msgid "<0>-lik</0>: like it, or having it."
msgstr "<0>-lik</0>: like it, or having it."

msgid "<0>-tu</0> and <1>-ke</1> usually join the genitive: <2>viga, vea, veatu</2>. Before <3>-lik</3> the stem varies: <4>sõbra-lik</4> but <5>oht-lik</5>. Pick an ending and tap the words."
msgstr "<0>-tu</0> and <1>-ke</1> usually join the genitive: <2>viga, vea, veatu</2>. Before <3>-lik</3> the stem varies: <4>sõbra-lik</4> but <5>oht-lik</5>. Pick an ending and tap the words."

msgid "<0>-tu</0> gives an adjective the same meaning as the case ending <1>-ta</1> from lesson {without}: <2>koer on koduta</2> and <3>kodutu koer</3> both describe a dog without a home."
msgstr "<0>-tu</0> gives an adjective the same meaning as the case ending <1>-ta</1> from lesson {without}: <2>koer on koduta</2> and <3>kodutu koer</3> both describe a dog without a home."

msgid "<0>-tu</0> means without, and usually joins the genitive: <1>kodutu, töötu, veatu</1>."
msgstr "<0>-tu</0> means without, and usually joins the genitive: <1>kodutu, töötu, veatu</1>."

msgid "<0>-tu</0> means without, like English -less. It usually joins the genitive."
msgstr "<0>-tu</0> means without, like English -less. It usually joins the genitive."

msgid "<0>-tu</0>: without it."
msgstr "<0>-tu</0>: without it."

